# Runs the support-flag probe on python: the one target CI can execute that has
# UDP but no CSPRNG, which is the combination where a support flag can lie.
#
# StunClient.isSupported said true there while the first line of discover()
# threw -- the exact bug class DatagramSocket.isSupported documents from the
# neko days, and the reason this is a run step rather than an assertion in a
# suite: every suite CI runs has a CSPRNG, so on those targets the invariant
# cannot fail and a test of it would be a vacuous control.
#
# Run it with `python export/python-support/flagprobe.py` once built.
-cp src
-cp tests/support
-main FlagProbe
-python export/python-support/flagprobe.py
